# A poster: big squares in a diamond, each with a small square inside, and words.
#   ./intent svg examples/art/poster.intent --after "wait 100" --style blocks
# The board is cut into blocks six cells across; how many blocks a block is from the middle one
# (across plus down) decides its colour, and the middle of every block gets a colour of its own.

The board is 42 wide and 54 high.
The background is sea green.
Cells have an x (number), a y (number), a block (number), a look (text) and a hue (text).
At the start there is a cell for every x from 0 to 41 and every y from 0 to 53, whose block is 0, whose look is " " and whose hue is "white".

Every 100 milliseconds, set the block of each cell to the absolute value of (its x divided by 6 minus 3) plus the absolute value of (its y divided by 6 minus 4).
Every 100 milliseconds, set the look of each cell to "#" if its block is under 3 and its y is at least 12, otherwise " ".
Every 100 milliseconds, set the hue of each cell to "white smoke" if its x modulo 6 is between 2 and 3 and its y modulo 6 is between 2 and 3 and its block is not 1, otherwise "dark orange" if its x modulo 6 is between 2 and 3 and its y modulo 6 is between 2 and 3, otherwise "dark orange" if its block is 0, otherwise "antique white" if its block is 1, otherwise "deep sky blue".

Draw each cell as its look in its hue at its x plus 1 and its y plus 1.
Write "Pictures" at 3 and 3 in white.
Write "in plain English" at 3 and 5 in white.
Write "sines, squares," at 3 and 49 in white.
Write "and sentences" at 3 and 51 in white.
Write "intent" at 34 and 51 in white.
